Use a 1% brightness step instead of 5%.

ashell hardcodes the step at 5% of max with no configuration knob; upstream has
no `brightness_step` setting. On windy's panel max is 528, so a 5% step is 26
raw units and the usable low end is a single press wide: sitting at 26, one
press down lands on zero. 1% gives 100 steps across the range and enough
resolution to actually settle on a comfortable level at night.

`.max(1)` already guards small-range backlights, so a panel whose max is under
100 still moves by one unit per press rather than stalling.

Recheck against src/modules/settings/brightness.rs on every ashell bump.

--- a/src/modules/settings/brightness.rs
+++ b/src/modules/settings/brightness.rs
@@ -45,7 +45,7 @@
     }
 
     fn step(max: u32) -> u32 {
-        (5 * max / 100).max(1)
+        (max / 100).max(1)
     }
 
     pub fn brightness_adjust(&mut self, up: bool) -> Action {
